Rename or copy this file to `PAUSE` (no extension) in this directory to stop the
daily newsroom agent.

    cp content/news/PAUSE.example content/news/PAUSE
    git add content/news/PAUSE && git commit -m "Pause the newsroom" && git push

The agent checks for `content/news/PAUSE` as the very first thing it does on every
run. If the file is present it publishes nothing, appends a `paused` line to
docs/newsroom/log.md, and exits.

Delete the file and push to resume.

This exists because the agent publishes to production with no review gate, so
stopping it must be one commit and must not require access to any schedule.
